values ('c3d4e5f6-7a8b-4c33-8d23-3e4f5a6b7c43', 'employment-law', 'Employment Law', 'This course prepares undergraduate Human Resources students to understand and apply U.S. employment law in day-to-day HR practice. Students learn how workplace rules are created and enforced, how to spot legal issues early, how to document decisions, how to administer legally sensitive processes, and how to partner with counsel while preserving employee trust and organizational fairness.');

